.TH SDE-UPDATE 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sde-update \- Software Updater: review and install software updates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-update
[\fB--page\fR \fINAME\fR]
.br
.B sde-update
\fB--check\fR | \fB--history\fR | \fB--sources\fR
.br
.B sde-update
\fB--plan\fR \fIACTION\fR [\fIPACKAGE\fR...]
.br
.B sde-update
\fB--transaction\fR \fBrefresh\fR|\fBupgrade\fR
.br
.B sde-update
\fB--notifier\fR [\fB--once\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBSoftware Updater\fR (called SDE Update before Alpha 51) keeps the operating
system up to date: it shows the updates of the Debian packages in the local APT
cache and installs the ones you keep checked. Applications from Flathub and the
Snap Store are updated in \fBmerkadu\fR(1), the software center; when it is
installed, the up-to-date view offers \fBOpen Merkadu\fR. The read-only Python
APT model is adapted from Linux Mint's Update Manager (mintupdate) with its
original GPLv3+ copyright preserved; held packages are excluded and counted.
.PP
The window asks whether to install the updated software now. \fBDetails of
updates\fR is a tree of three groups, each with a check box (checked, unchecked
or mixed), its download size and its updates:
.TP
.B Critical updates
packages with Priority \fBrequired\fR or \fBimportant\fR, the kernel, the C
library, systemd, D-Bus, APT, dpkg, the boot loader, firmware and microcode,
updates whose changelog urgency is high or critical, and every update that
needs a restart.
.TP
.B Security updates
updates from the Debian security archive (the Debian-Security label or a
\fI*-security\fR suite).
.TP
.B Main updates
everything else from the package sources, backports included.
.PP
Updates show the application's name and icon when the package ships a desktop
file, otherwise the package's short description. \fBTechnical description\fR
shows the selected update's versions, origin, size and changelog
(\fBapt-get changelog\fR, then PackageKit's update details, then the installed
changelog), loaded in the background with a time limit. The line below tells
how much will be downloaded.
.PP
\fBInstall Now\fR installs the checked updates: all updates checked means a
full upgrade, otherwise \fBapt-get install --only-upgrade\fR (or PackageKit) of
the checked packages.
Progress, the current package and the log appear in the window; when a restart
is needed, \fBRestart Now\fR and \fBLater\fR are offered. \fBRemind Me Later\fR
closes the window and silences the notification for a day (see
\fBremind_hours\fR). \fBSettings…\fR opens the other pages with a sidebar:
\fBHistory\fR lists the transactions recorded in \fI/var/log/apt/history.log\fR
and its rotated copies. \fBSources\fR lists the entries of
\fI/etc/apt/sources.list\fR and \fI/etc/apt/sources.list.d\fR (one-line
\fI.list\fR and deb822 \fI.sources\fR files) read-only, and opens
software-properties-gtk when it is installed. \fBMaintenance\fR refreshes the
package lists, cleans the package cache, removes unused packages after showing
them, repairs interrupted installations and opens PackageKit's interactive
update in a terminal. \fBSettings\fR controls the automatic checks. Escape goes
back to the updater.
.PP
The window follows the SDE theme, including changes made while it is open.
.PP
Transactions run in a helper process and report per-package progress. They use
PackageKit (\fBpkcon\fR) when its daemon is available, which applies the
system's polkit policy and can be cancelled; otherwise, and for cleaning and
removing unused packages, \fBapt-get\fR runs through \fBpkexec\fR. Software
Updater never runs APT as root by itself, accepts no repository URLs or
options, and validates every package name.
.PP
Debian testing transitions can require manual APT decisions; a preview from the
local cache does not guarantee that every upgrade is currently resolvable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --page " NAME"
Open \fBupdates\fR (the updater), \fBhistory\fR, \fBsources\fR,
\fBmaintenance\fR, \fBsettings\fR or \fBabout\fR.
.TP
.B --check
Print the versioned tab-separated update list (SDE-UPDATES 2) and exit.
.TP
.B --history
Print the APT history (SDE-HISTORY 1) and exit.
.TP
.B --sources
Print the package sources (SDE-SOURCES 1) and exit.
.TP
.BI --plan " ACTION" " " [PACKAGE...]
Print the fixed argument vector of \fBrefresh\fR, \fBupgrade\fR,
\fBautoremove\fR, \fBclean\fR or \fBrepair\fR without running it.
.TP
.B --transaction refresh|upgrade
Run the interactive PackageKit operation in the current terminal.
.TP
.B --notifier \fR[\fB--once\fR]
Check for updates in the background and show a notification. Started at login
from \fI/etc/xdg/autostart/sde-update-notifier.desktop\fR; \fB--once\fR checks
immediately and exits.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The \fB[update]\fR section of \fIsde.conf\fR:
.TP
.B check_interval
Hours between automatic checks: 0 (never), 1, 6, 12, 24 or 168.
.TP
.B auto_refresh
Refresh the package lists through PackageKit before automatic checks, and when
the window opens with outdated lists.
.TP
.B notify\fR, \fBnotify_security_only
Show a notification for available updates (only critical and security ones).
.TP
.B remind_hours
How long \fBRemind Me Later\fR silences the notification: 1, 4, 24 (default),
72 or 168 hours.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/sde/update/
helpers: check.py, model.py, history.py, sources.py, changelog.py,
transaction.py
.br
.I ~/.local/state/sde/update-notifier
time of the last automatic check and the end of Remind Me Later
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkcon (1),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR merkadu (1),
.BR sde-suite (1),
.BR apt-get (8)
